{
	"$comment": [
		"Licences of what the website is built from and serves, checked on every build by scripts/third-party-licenses.mjs,",
		"which also writes public/third-party-licenses.txt from them. The top level is for npm packages, \"python\" for the",
		"Python wheels the playground serves. Only permissive licences (and the OFL, for the fonts) are allowed for every",
		"package; anything else is a decision about one package, recorded with its reason.",
		"An entry applies to the package named by its key, or to every package starting with it if it ends in *.",
		"'declared' is the licence exactly as the package states it: if a release states anything else, the entry no",
		"longer applies and the build fails until someone reads the new licence. 'license' replaces a declared licence",
		"that is not SPDX; 'allow' allows more licences for this package only; 'source' is where the source code of the",
		"served version is, for licences that ask the site to say so (MPL-2.0).",
		"'texts' are upstream licence and NOTICE texts the package does not ship, saved in licenses/ from 'from' (where",
		"{version} is the package's version, {python} and {emscripten} Pyodide's). They were saved for 'version': when",
		"the package changes version, the build fails until `npm run vendor-licenses` refetches them, for review.",
		"'notServed' says why a package that ships no licence text needs none here: nothing of it reaches the site. The build checks it",
		"(scripts/served-packages.mjs): it fails if a module of such a package is bundled for the browser, or a file of the built site is a copy of one of its files.",
		"'components' lists what upstream compiled into the package's served files, as recipes vendor-licenses.mjs resolves",
		"(from upstream's build files and lockfiles, at the served version) into 'manifest'. With 'binary', every symbol the",
		"package's WebAssembly exports must belong to a component ('symbols'), to the package ('ownSymbols'), or to the",
		"reviewed C runtime list ('runtimeSymbols'), so a library linked in without its licence fails the build.",
		"'textsFrom': 'pypi' takes a Python package's licence files from its PyPI release at the served version.",
		"'componentTexts' gives the text of a component whose release ships none, by 'name@version' (so a new version is reviewed again): a URL at",
		"an immutable commit or tag, or 'spdx:<ID>' when no text exists upstream at all: the SPDX standard text of the declared licence, with the",
		"author its package.json names as the holder, marked as reconstructed in the report."
	],
	"allowed": [
		"0BSD",
		"Apache-2.0",
		"BlueOak-1.0.0",
		"BSD-2-Clause",
		"BSD-3-Clause",
		"CC0-1.0",
		"ISC",
		"MIT",
		"OFL-1.1"
	],
	"exceptions": [
		"LLVM-exception"
	],
