					"hifijson@0.5.0": [
						"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/01mf02/hifijson/91e6e0639e321f7d2d1e28c0eefb4a9fe6dbad33/LICENSE-MIT"
					],
					"pagefind_stem@1.0.0": [
						"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pagefind/pagefind/eb1a6711c45c78d9b536fad167650a79f9a97a5c/LICENSE",
						"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/CurrySoftware/rust-stemmers/1fde09dfa08fb0fb07fbd6570aba8ecc98174edb/LICENSE",
						"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/snowballstem/snowball/v3.0.0/COPYING"
					],
					"is-reference@3.0.3": [
						"spdx:MIT"
					],
					"locate-character@3.0.0": [
						"spdx:MIT"
					]
				},
				"$comment": "componentTexts, for components whose release ships no licence file: hifijson 0.5.0 (MIT): LICENSE-MIT from the commit its author added it in, right after the 0.5.0 bump, changing nothing else. pagefind_stem 1.0.0 (MIT): published from Pagefind commit eb1a6711 (its .cargo_vcs_info.json), so Pagefind's LICENSE there; its API derives from rust-stemmers (MIT, notice in its lib.rs) and its algorithms are generated by Snowball 3.0.0 (BSD-3-Clause), so their licences too. is-reference 3.0.3 and locate-character 3.0.0 (Svelte's dependencies): no licence file in any release or ever in their repositories, only \"license\": \"MIT\" and the author in package.json, so the SPDX MIT text with that author ('spdx:MIT')."
			}
		},
